From b843cf07f851985413c926a562f9135a272a3bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hao Lin <hao.lin@samsung.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:27:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [llvm-profgen] Enumerate instruction boundaries on demand for
 IP samples

Enumerate sampled DWARF ranges using section-local ARM/AArch64 mapping symbols and runtime instruction bytes. Add average aggregation, sampled-function zero filling, previous-instruction skid adjustment, and deterministic boundary diagnostics with tests.

Repair three AArch64 inputs that used .byte for instructions and accidentally introduced conflicting data mappings; .inst preserves the code bytes and existing boundary goldens.

Keep skid predecessors within one mapping interval and require usable predecessor line information. Report unadjusted reasons and group sampled addresses by function before validating boundaries.
