+#===- boundary-extra - Symbolized copies of patch1 fixtures ----------------===#
+# Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
+# See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
+#===----------------------------------------------------------------------===#
+Patch1 manual fixtures have function ranges but no line tables. These copies
+add only DW_AT_stmt_list, DW_AT_decl_line=1 and a DWARF4 line table. Machine
+bytes, mapping symbols and function ranges are unchanged. No golden was read
+from llvm-profgen: boundary-golden.json is the independent patch1 oracle.
+Byte rows: raw line=1+(address-anchor), decl_line=1. Two *-uniform copies instead
+map every byte to line1 for avg's whole-function and discontiguous denominators.
+a64-no-map uses .inst, then llvm-objcopy --globalize-symbol='$x' on the
+linked file; the non-local $x must not count as a mapping symbol.
+Reproduce each .s with platform clang --target=armv7l-tizen-linux-gnueabi
+(or --target=aarch64-tizen-linux-gnu for *a64*) -c; ld.lld -shared --build-id=sha1 -z max-page-size=4096 -Ttext=0x1000.
+section-adjacent uses ../section-adjacent.lds instead of -Ttext.
+boundaries.debug uses llvm-objcopy --only-keep-debug; stripped uses --strip-all.
+
+Exact reproduction (run from this directory; .s files already contain all DWARF):
+Tools: Tizen clang/LLD/llvm-objcopy 22.1.8, GNU readelf 2.43.
+AArch64 root: temp/GBS-ROOT-RPI5-SPIKE/local/BUILD-ROOTS/scratch.aarch64.0/emul
+ARM root: temp/GBS-ROOT-V04-FFMPEG/local/BUILD-ROOTS/scratch.armv7l.0/emul
+Both paths are relative to the project WORKDIR. Launch each tool using its root's
+lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --library-path ROOT/lib64:ROOT/usr/lib64 ROOT/usr/bin/TOOL.
+For every NAME.s, use that architecture's tool launcher for these commands:
+  clang --target=TARGET -c NAME.s -o WORKDIR/temp/profgen-patch5/fixtures/NAME.o
+  ld.lld -shared --build-id=sha1 -z max-page-size=4096 -Ttext=0x1000 \
+    WORKDIR/temp/profgen-patch5/fixtures/NAME.o -o NAME.perfbin
+For section-adjacent only, replace -Ttext=0x1000 with -T ../section-adjacent.lds.
+For a64-no-map only, then run llvm-objcopy --globalize-symbol='$x' a64-no-map.perfbin.
+For boundaries, also run:
+  llvm-objcopy --only-keep-debug boundaries.perfbin boundaries.debug
+  llvm-objcopy --strip-all boundaries.perfbin boundaries.stripped.perfbin
+
+NAME list (TARGET=armv7l-tizen-linux-gnueabi unless noted):
+  boundaries, boundary-before_state, boundary-at_state, boundary-discontinuous,
+  boundary-after_data_a32, pure-arm, arm-literal, section-adjacent,
+  bad-thumb-start, bad-thumb-end, bad-arm-start, bad-conflict, bad-no-map,
+  discontinuous-uniform, arm-uniform.
+TARGET=aarch64-tizen-linux-gnu:
+  pure-a64, bad-a64-start, bad-a64-end, a64-no-map.
+
+The patch1 pure-a64/bad-a64-start/bad-a64-end originals were corrected in patch5
+from .byte plus handwritten $x to identical .inst bytes and assembler-generated
+$x. This prevents the AArch64 assembler's automatic $d from conflicting with $x.
+Original golden addresses and all function ranges are unchanged. bad-conflict
+remains a dedicated same-address, different-state negative input.
+
+Patch5 follow-up: skid-no-line.s derives boundaries.s without changing code or ranges.
+The initial .debug_line row has line 0 at 0x1000; the second instruction
+at 0x1002 keeps line 3. This proves that prev-inst must retain 0x1002 when
+its predecessor lacks usable line information. Build with the ARM commands
+above, substituting skid-no-line for boundaries (clang/LLD 22.1.8).
